icants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURARAY CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITANI TOSHIMICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUJI YOSHIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURARAY CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITANI, TOSHIMICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJI, YOSHIHISA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITANI TOSHIMICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUJI YOSHIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITANI, TOSHIMICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJI, YOSHIHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Steroid derivatives useful as the intermediate for preparing vitamin D derivatives such as 1 alpha , 25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 and 2 beta -(3-hydroxypropoxy)-1 alpha , 25-dihydroxyvitamin D3, i.e., halides of general formula (II) (wherein X is bromo or iodo); 1,4,6-trien-3-one compounds of general formula (III) (wherein X is as defined above); 1,3,5,7-tetraene compounds of general formula (IV) (wherein X is as defined above; and R&lt;1&gt; is acyl); and 1,5,7-triene compounds of general formula (V) (wherein X is as defined above; and R&lt;2&gt; is hydrogen or a hydroxyl-protecting group); and processes for the preparation of the same.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur des dérivés de stéroïdes utiles comme intermédiaires dans la préparation de dérivés de la vitamine D tels que 1 alpha , 25-dihydroxyvitamine D3 et 2 beta -(3-hydroxypropoxy)-1 alpha , 25-dihydroxyvitamine D3, c'est-à-dire des halogénures de la formule générale (II) (dans laquelle X représente brome ou iode); des composés 1,4,6-trien-3-one de la formule générale (III) (dans laquelle X est tel que précité); des composés 1,3,5,7-tétraène de la formule générale (IV) (dans laquelle X est tel que précité et où R&lt;1&gt; est un acyle); et des composés 1,5,7-triène de la formule générale (V) (dans laquelle X est tel que précité; et où R&lt;2&gt; représente hydrogène ou un groupe protégeant hydroxyle). L'invention porte également sur des procédés de préparation de ces composés.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>